From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:50:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 37/38] isolate: align runtime acceptance fixtures with the
 invocation ABI

Issue the synchronous normalization capability only after provider preparation and pass typed version-4 capability requests through the production codec. Retain stale-identity and transferred-operand checks, and set the operation budget to the six operations exercised before the limit assertion.

Account for the canonical URL configuration read performed before handler execution. Compare complete dependencies against initialization on the same snapshot, including derived table/index dependencies, so malformed queries and ID-only operations still prove they made no additional reads.

Validation: the feature-enabled runtime acceptance suite passes 34 tests with three external-artifact tests explicitly ignored. No production runtime behavior changes.
